**Why it fails the gap test.** He has a personal Wikipedia page, IMDb's dedicated bio, a Biography.com feature, Premiere Speakers, Grokipedia, *and two official bios he controls himself* (`natebargatze.com/bio`, `nateland.com/pages/nate`). The general-biography surface is more thoroughly served than Bill Burr's was. Flat −20 penalty, subtotal 61 → 41.

**Why it's still worth writing.** The psychology SERP is emptier than Burr's — Burr had seven typology properties and a contested debate; Bargatze has boo.world, personalitylist, a hijacked `monitor.biology.washington.edu` WordPress subdomain, and three name collisions (Big Nate, Nate Archibald, Nate Jacobs). Nobody has staked the query.

**The angle is fresher than I expected.** Two dated character tests, both unwritten psychologically:
- **The Breadwinner** (2026-05-29, his co-written feature debut) — 19–20% RT critics vs. **86% audience, CinemaScore A−**. Critics didn't say it was badly made; they said it was *too clean*. THR: "inoffensive to the point of total boredom." The identity itself got named as the defect.
- **The Emmys donation bit** (2025-09) — ended the night at **−$60,000**; he paid $250k he says on his own podcast he never planned to pay rather than let the bit die in public.

Organizing contradiction: the "Greatest Average American" persona is the marketing surface of a theme-park-scale empire plan — Nashville production facility, clean-comic talent incubator, branded cruise, feature film, two self-owned bio pages.

**One thing you should see before drafting.** I pulled the comedian cluster's actual GSC numbers and the pattern is not good: Tina Fey (1,711 imps, pos 7.3), Rogan (947), Noah (650) all shipped **March–April 2025**. All six comedian pages shipped since December 2025 — Schulz, Kreischer, Chappelle, Theo Von, Gillis, Rife — sit at or near zero, three absent from the export entirely. Whatever worked last spring hasn't reproduced. I wrote the prediction as a 56–90 day ramp, not 28, and flagged that if drafting can't land the contradiction this page joins the zero half of the cluster.

